        {
          "path": "_m/r/c/k/b/hobbiton-movie-set-wp/an-old-well-hobbiton-movie-set.jpg",
          "filename": "An Old Well, Hobbiton Movie Set, Matamata, New Zealand 2016 (50797299096).jpg",
          "caption": "A non-functioning well, this is one of the props for the movies.A scene from our tour of the Hobbiton set, made famous in the \"Lord of the Rings\" movie series.  Located on the Alexander Sheep Farm near Matamata, New Zealand, the 12 acre movie set is a must-see for fans and is a delight for those who aren't familiar with the movies, too.  44 permanently constructed Hobbit Holes are on the site, as well as the Green Dragon Inn.  Anything outside of a Hobbit Hole is artificial; a prop for the movie.\nIt was springtime in the Shire when we visited.  Baby Lambs were bounding everywhere.\n\nSeptember, 2016",
          "alt": "A non-functioning well, this is one of the props for the movies.A scene from our tour of the Hobbiton set, made famous in the \"Lord of the Rings\" movie series.  Located on the Alexander Sheep Farm near Matamata, New Zealand, the 12 acre movie set is a must-see for fans and is a delight for those who aren't familiar with the movies, too.  44 permanently constructed Hobbit Holes are on the site, as well as the Green Dragon Inn.  Anything outside of a Hobbit Hole is artificial; a prop for the movie.\nIt was springtime in the Shire when we visited.  Baby Lambs were bounding everywhere.\n\nSeptember, 2016",
          "width": 3696,
          "height": 2448,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Joe Ross from Lansing, Michigan",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An_Old_Well,_Hobbiton_Movie_Set,_Matamata,_New_Zealand_2016_(50797299096).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "hobbiton-movie-set-wp",
