        {
          "path": "_m/r/c/k/b/hobbiton-movie-set-wp/a-view-of-hobbiton-from-the-gr.jpg",
          "filename": "A view of Hobbiton from the Green Dragon Inn, Hobbiton Movie Set, Matamata, New Zealand 2016 (50796593188).jpg",
          "caption": "As we leave the Green Dragon Inn to head to the shuttle bus, we get a view across the mill pond to Hobbiton.  The Party tree is the large tree on the right near the water.\nA scene from our tour of the Hobbiton set, made famous in the \"Lord of the Rings\" movie series.  Located on the Alexander Sheep Farm near Matamata, New Zealand, the 12 acre movie set is a must-see for fans and is a delight for those who aren't familiar with the movies, too.  44 permanently constructed Hobbit Holes are on the site, as well as the Green Dragon Inn.  Anything outside of a Hobbit Hole is artificial; a prop for the movie.\nIt was springtime in the Shire when we visited.  Baby Lambs were bounding everywhere.\n\nSeptember, 2016",
